s:48532:"{
"lastpushid": 1568,
"pushes": {"137": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 7e770707fe156fc2e62c5f624235e4b2dadc1e7b with FIREFOX_115_4_0esr_BUILD1 a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9e8b4a820f3202e3c2c36f195869cc87b4cfd454", "parents": ["7e770707fe156fc2e62c5f624235e4b2dadc1e7b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1697511433, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "138": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Update configs. IGNORE BROKEN CHANGESETS CLOSED TREE NO BUG a=release ba=release", "files": ["CLOBBER", "browser/config/version.txt", "browser/config/version_display.txt", "config/milestone.txt"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5545a69ca145ea354f01c4c95e79baef7e69802d", "parents": ["9e8b4a820f3202e3c2c36f195869cc87b4cfd454"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698071620, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld-merge"}, "139": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 7e770707fe156fc2e62c5f624235e4b2dadc1e7b with FIREFOX_115_4_0esr_RELEASE a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4cc465ee3061be6b90b01ea6b9a02de3915e407d", "parents": ["5545a69ca145ea354f01c4c95e79baef7e69802d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698152322, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "140": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr115 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings tld-suffixes - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191634", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/cookie-banner-rules-list.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "55428fae0a066c5fca921627f5893fb55f56c769", "parents": ["4cc465ee3061be6b90b01ea6b9a02de3915e407d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1818419 - Intermittent netwerk/test/unit/test_dooh.js caused by TTL refresh on windows r=necko-reviewers,jesup a=test-only\n\nThe TTL refresh is done asynchronously with low priority on windows.\nWhen clearing the cache between tests, this callback may still exist\nso it may refresh the cache entry with the native value instead of the TRR one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191399", "files": ["netwerk/test/unit/test_dooh.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c54d0d4c35042812bcd752bf1e51f6a161e2abd8", "parents": ["55428fae0a066c5fca921627f5893fb55f56c769"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1776767 - Skip failing GMP tests on Windows ASAN. r=alwu, a=test-only\n\nUntil we can resolve the underlying bug which is causing GMP launch\nslowdowns on Windows ASAN builds, just skip the impacted tests.", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestCDMStorage.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestGMPCrossOrigin.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cfc3ea85cd566c058577a07bb453a3390ace1e55", "parents": ["c54d0d4c35042812bcd752bf1e51f6a161e2abd8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Creskey \u003cacreskey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1843384 - Crash in [@ shutdownhang | mozilla::net::nsSocketTransportService::SetOffline] r=valentin,necko-reviewers a=RyanVM\n\nWe abort the re-initialization of the socketTransportService during shutdown to prevent a deadlock.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D187915", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsIOService.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3a69c91f76e419749a8fe22089ec98720829b533", "parents": ["cfc3ea85cd566c058577a07bb453a3390ace1e55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Creskey \u003cacreskey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1843384 - Crash in [@ shutdownhang | mozilla::net::nsSocketTransportService::SetOffline] r=valentin,necko-reviewers a=RyanVM\n\nWe avoid blocking the main thread by allocating the PollableEvent outside the mutex. Still has the potential to hang the socket thread, but the main thread remains responsive.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D188512", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsSocketTransportService2.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "63606b36f19d35177d60cdc4e74b4d7b448c855e", "parents": ["3a69c91f76e419749a8fe22089ec98720829b533"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1852849 - Make `HTMLEditor::AutoInlineStyleSetter::ExtendOrShrinkRangeToApplyTheStyle` recompute common ancestor of the range if it updates the range r=m_kato a=RyanVM\n\nIn this case, `\u003cfont face=\"monospace\"\u003eabc []\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/font\u003e`, the range applying\nnew style will be extended as `\u003cfont face=\"monospace\"\u003eabc [\u003cbr\u003e}\u003c/font\u003e` first.\nhttps://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/29bdf6ff9965a647c6f64d63fed2b5bd094532c7/editor/libeditor/HTMLStyleEditor.cpp#1944\n\nThen, the start point should be shrunken and the range should become\n`\u003cfont face=\"monospace\"\u003eabc {\u003cbr\u003e}\u003c/font\u003e`.\nhttps://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/29bdf6ff9965a647c6f64d63fed2b5bd094532c7/editor/libeditor/HTMLStyleEditor.cpp#1977-1978\n\nHowever, `commonAncestor` is still the text node because it's not updated\nafter extending the range to include the `\u003cbr\u003e`.  Then,\n`AutoInlineStyleSetter::GetNextEditableInlineContent` fails to get `\u003cbr\u003e`\nfrom the text node.\nhttps://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/29bdf6ff9965a647c6f64d63fed2b5bd094532c7/editor/libeditor/HTMLStyleEditor.cpp#1576-1578\n\nFinally, the unexpected range computation will reach here with the text editor\nand adjust the start of the range to start of the text node.\nhttps://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/29bdf6ff9965a647c6f64d63fed2b5bd094532c7/editor/libeditor/HTMLStyleEditor.cpp#420-423\n\nTherefore, the new text which the new style should be applied is jumped to\nstart of the text node.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D190028", "files": ["editor/libeditor/HTMLStyleEditor.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/editing/other/inserttext-after-bold-in-font-face-monospace.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "03f4ed2f206d23d966286a75978846d8ca1f8d75", "parents": ["63606b36f19d35177d60cdc4e74b4d7b448c855e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1859591 - Add gfxCriticalNote when failing to load EGL/GLES DLLs on Windows. r=gfx-reviewers,jrmuizel a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191206", "files": ["gfx/gl/GLLibraryEGL.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c900bad131294eb3fdb29138411e480fe27e0fd7", "parents": ["03f4ed2f206d23d966286a75978846d8ca1f8d75"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698172162, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "141": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "FIREFOX_ESR_115_3_X_RELBRANCH", "desc": "Close obsolete FIREFOX_ESR_115_3_X_RELBRANCH. a=release", "files": [], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "aeaf462e36c838f014e345f64a6c0c529b591164", "parents": ["749617c4473c65f8aebb2e3254777ae99dc17cce"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698339334, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "142": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr115 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings tld-suffixes - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191950", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/devtools-compatibility-browsers.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/search-telemetry-v2.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2cba3f6469de960574dcb57e60dd88a70082d6a5", "parents": ["c900bad131294eb3fdb29138411e480fe27e0fd7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gregory Pappas \u003cgp3033@protonmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1854298 - Implement PrintingEnabled policy. r=emilio,mkaply,Gijs,fluent-reviewers a=RyanVM", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/policies/policies-descriptions.ftl", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/components/printing/tests/browser.ini", "toolkit/components/printing/tests/browser_print_disabled.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ab54885670e505b900bb92602526f4420ebe441b", "parents": ["2cba3f6469de960574dcb57e60dd88a70082d6a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1859595 - Allow preferences that begin with pref. in policy. r=kcochrane, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191209", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "08378e605d8dc5f0b30da625cd836fb99c65882c", "parents": ["ab54885670e505b900bb92602526f4420ebe441b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698341119, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "143": {"changesets": [{"author": "James Teow \u003cjteow@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1836156 - Remove extraPageRegexps from search-telemetry-v2 - r=Standard8, a=RyanVM", "files": ["browser/components/search/SearchSERPTelemetry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/search/test/browser/browser_search_telemetry_engagement_content.js", "browser/components/search/test/unit/test_search_telemetry_config_validation.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "adfeede21af2b7198f2c19b32aa93c119236154f", "parents": ["08378e605d8dc5f0b30da625cd836fb99c65882c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teow \u003cjteow@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1853004 - Add ad_image_row to ad components - r=Standard8, a=RyanVM", "files": ["browser/components/search/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/search/schema/search-telemetry-schema.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9800392efc7f0ef68c87382be8cf3bda208daf18", "parents": ["adfeede21af2b7198f2c19b32aa93c119236154f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860531 - Add new queryParamNames option to search-telemetry-v2 schema for specifying multiple query parameter names. r=search-reviewers,jteow a=RyanVM\n\nThis is a new option that allows specifying multiple query parameter names, so that we can support\nsome search engines on mobile, where they use a different parameter name to desktop.\n\nA future changeset will make 'queryParamNames' a required parameter.", "files": ["browser/components/search/schema/search-telemetry-schema.json", "browser/components/search/schema/search-telemetry-ui-schema.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "0389f90059987697472119e604c90c1d9ed678f2", "parents": ["9800392efc7f0ef68c87382be8cf3bda208daf18"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karandeep \u003cklubana@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1856984 - Update daum-kr Search Engine Configuration. r=Standard8, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D190314", "files": ["browser/components/search/extensions/daum-kr/manifest.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "72fdd79924115eec29cdf9e3c37d98b7070e76ee", "parents": ["0389f90059987697472119e604c90c1d9ed678f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karandeep \u003cklubana@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1856985 - Update Salidzini.lv Search Engine Configuration. r=Standard8, a=RyanVM", "files": ["browser/components/search/extensions/salidzinilv/manifest.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ce7012a252b1b53d9db06983f95a41475d888246", "parents": ["72fdd79924115eec29cdf9e3c37d98b7070e76ee"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698424229, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "144": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1843534 - Remove unused telemetry probes.  a=diannaS\n\nThese telemetry probes have long since expired, so remove them. This\navoids taking unnecessary timestamps in these functions, which we have\nseen can be expensive on certain devices.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D185007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192116", "files": ["layout/base/nsRefreshDriver.cpp", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json", "xpcom/ds/nsObserverService.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cb731d48619e9b319e824de2c1a68e927aa25545", "parents": ["ce7012a252b1b53d9db06983f95a41475d888246"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1861259 part 1: Refactor out a helper function for loop body in nsRefreshDriver::Tick.  a=diannaS\n\nThis doesn't affect behavior; it's just a pure refactoring, moving code from\nbeing inline to being in a helper function.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191908\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191985", "files": ["layout/base/nsRefreshDriver.cpp", "layout/base/nsRefreshDriver.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3e67c049c9d532891cdf73551055000bae1cde2d", "parents": ["cb731d48619e9b319e824de2c1a68e927aa25545"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1861259 part 2: Unroll the observer-array-loop in nsRefreshDriver::Tick.  a=diannaS\n\nThis patch doesn't change behavior.\n\nThis is a bit gross, but it helps us make better use of the backtrace to figure\nout what's going on in a given crash report.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191909\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191986", "files": ["layout/base/nsRefreshDriver.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9044fbb8cfd02250a90a9d32a00ac9bf526932f4", "parents": ["3e67c049c9d532891cdf73551055000bae1cde2d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1861259 part 3: Coalesce redundant array-index checks in nsRefreshDriver.  a=diannaS\n\nThis patch doesn't change behavior; it just removes some redundant checks.\n\n(Note that the tight-scoping around nsAutoMicroTask/ReduceAnimations is\nimportant for the RAII object to be torn down at the intended time; but it\ndoesn't need its own if-check.)\n\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191911\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191987", "files": ["layout/base/nsRefreshDriver.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b3b57a7219e9b42cbc0533ec682086afc47b3d23", "parents": ["9044fbb8cfd02250a90a9d32a00ac9bf526932f4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698464377, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "145": {"changesets": [{"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1855345 - Make `AutoCopyListener` ignore any selection changes caused by Selection API r=karlt,smaug, a=dsmith\n\nEven though there is a reasonable usabe like bug 1567160, we should\nensure that `AutoCopyListener` never update clipboard when the selection\nchange is caused by a Selection API call.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191585", "files": ["layout/generic/nsFrameSelection.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "db1c17fea00f483edcca7fd808a8387ff34bf4dc", "parents": ["b3b57a7219e9b42cbc0533ec682086afc47b3d23"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brad Werth \u003cbwerth@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1658432: Don't remove wrapping CALayer from its superview outside of Commit. r=mac-reviewers,mstange, a=dsmith\n\nThis change lets NativeLayerRootCA::Representation::Commit be the only\npoint where sublayers are added and removed from the root CALayer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191673", "files": ["gfx/layers/NativeLayerCA.mm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cf8c7fe2deeb5ceea61cee515fd9111afd8f9883", "parents": ["db1c17fea00f483edcca7fd808a8387ff34bf4dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1859030 - Exit early in WorkerManagerCreatedRunnable::Run if the actor cannot send. r=dom-worker-reviewers,asuth, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191094", "files": ["dom/workers/sharedworkers/SharedWorkerService.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a301997400cc0a684834b1c3812eabdc5f60ad8c", "parents": ["cf8c7fe2deeb5ceea61cee515fd9111afd8f9883"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr115 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings tld-suffixes - a=repo-update, r=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192200", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "edb25f5aa1c08b7067f97c99db9a27669d0a84df", "parents": ["a301997400cc0a684834b1c3812eabdc5f60ad8c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698672831, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "146": {"changesets": [{"author": "Botond Ballo \u003cbotond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1777416 - Avoid GetStateForRoot() incorrectly returning a non-root LayerTreeState.  a=diannaS\n\nIn the case where the LayerTreeState for the input content LayersID\nwas found, but its mParent was null for some reason, the function\nwas incorrectly returning the content LayerTreeState.\n\nInstead, in such a case, where the root LayerTreeState cannot be\nlooked up, the function should return null.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D190143\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192278", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "109022183d59495cfc3b5a95d5c3177aa0c8146a", "parents": ["edb25f5aa1c08b7067f97c99db9a27669d0a84df"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698702487, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "147": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kelsey Gilbert \u003ckelsey.gilbert@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1841050 - Add pref webgl.gl_khr_no_error:true. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth, a=dsmith\n\nThis allows for disabling WebGL's use of GL_KHR_no_error, rather than the default of enabled.\n\nUse snake_case so that searching for KHR_no_error finds this more\neasily.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D188781", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLContext.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "76f91cb28fdfa8e8438e493a364b2353d2280539", "parents": ["109022183d59495cfc3b5a95d5c3177aa0c8146a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kelsey Gilbert \u003ckelsey.gilbert@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1841050 - Disable webgl.gl_khr_no_error on Windows. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D188782", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "feb44fb3185ba35ac752fddbe80ecc45e7f0b6c2", "parents": ["76f91cb28fdfa8e8438e493a364b2353d2280539"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1841050. r=gfx-reviewers,nical,ahale , a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191597", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLTextureUpload.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "7560222f64ed3ee0860d21f79d39043e99996810", "parents": ["feb44fb3185ba35ac752fddbe80ecc45e7f0b6c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1841050. Mark expected test fail. r=gfx-reviewers,nical,ahale, a=dsmith\n\nDepends on D191597\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191598", "files": ["dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/generated-mochitest.ini", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/mochitest-errata.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e0a921d60bd50a79846c9bf8602920238a579bc8", "parents": ["7560222f64ed3ee0860d21f79d39043e99996810"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860001: Handle invalid events. r=eeejay, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191601", "files": ["accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleParent.cpp", "accessible/windows/msaa/MsaaAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c7af04b3795ecbddf34ca09b44baf6ad30550b86", "parents": ["e0a921d60bd50a79846c9bf8602920238a579bc8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Betterbird \u003cbetterbird@betterbird.eu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1856189 - Use selectedIndex setter on wizard. a=dsmith\n\nSetting the \"selectedIndex\" attribute doesn't trigger all the relevant\nside effects. It's also simpler.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D189766", "files": ["toolkit/content/widgets/wizard.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c528c13ff29a6dc072af09bdd8c5adc072a1c8be", "parents": ["c7af04b3795ecbddf34ca09b44baf6ad30550b86"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860943 - Hold mutex before accessing mAnimation. r=botond, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191813", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/AsyncPanZoomController.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/AsyncPanZoomController.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "12c320c1384d8b09a6d81c55e2ea786dfc1c877b", "parents": ["c528c13ff29a6dc072af09bdd8c5adc072a1c8be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1859458: Never try to cast a XUL TableAccessible to a CachedTableAccessible. r=morgan, a=dsmith\n\nThis is a speculative crash fix; I don't know how to reproduce this problem.\nA non-XUL (HTML, SVG, etc.) table cell should always have a CachedTableAccessible ancestor.\nApparently, this sometimes isn't the case.\nIt seems there can be a table ancestor which is not a CachedTableAccessible, which could only be a XULListboxAccessible or XULTreeGridAccessible.\nIn this case, CachedTableCellAccessible::GetFrom would previously try to cast this TableAccessible to a CachedTableAccessible and breakage would ensue.\nI don't know how this can happen, but we protect against this now by returning early if a XUL table is found, since a XUL table can never be a CachedTableAccessible.\nIn contrast, all non-XUL tables are always CachedTableAccessibles.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191374", "files": ["accessible/base/CachedTableAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "77c5994fb586d30cc56b8702669e074ae23e8d9f", "parents": ["12c320c1384d8b09a6d81c55e2ea786dfc1c877b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1818757 - Increase network triggering timeout in test_race_cache_with_network.js r=necko-reviewers,jesup, a=test-only\n\n100ms is probably too little and in some cases the cache may not be\nfast enough to fulfil the request - which is what the test is expecting.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191860", "files": ["netwerk/test/unit/test_race_cache_with_network.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "fff67dcdd705e18dd827bc14759a89ea8266d906", "parents": ["77c5994fb586d30cc56b8702669e074ae23e8d9f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698705653, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "148": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andrew Sutherland \u003casutherland@asutherland.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1854076 - ESR115 Improve MessagePort state machine. r=dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191773", "files": ["dom/messagechannel/MessagePort.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d04b0067e2ec64e290fc887c316e0b5ee6eb2b34", "parents": ["fff67dcdd705e18dd827bc14759a89ea8266d906"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698715216, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "149": {"changesets": [{"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1851041 - Ignore `CFSTR_FILEDESCRIPTOR*` if `text/x-moz-url` is present;  a=diannaS\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192316", "files": ["widget/windows/nsDragService.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b7029431868a853b7f9f82e3be9d8f2fc7a11540", "parents": ["d04b0067e2ec64e290fc887c316e0b5ee6eb2b34"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698761609, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "150": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860767 - Replace MOZ_ReportCrash call for AutoEnterOOMUnsafeRegion with fprintf. r=jonco, a=dsmith\n\nAccording to bug 1859737, there are some issues with the stack dumping code on Windows\nand the goal is to stop defining `MOZ_ReportCrash` in non-debug builds.\nFor `AutoEnterOOMUnsafeRegion` it seems simplest to do our own printf.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191735", "files": ["js/src/vm/JSContext.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c7af063f1aeae8d646aa65389042d18fb037505f", "parents": ["b7029431868a853b7f9f82e3be9d8f2fc7a11540"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1854090 - Omit psnames of fonts with family-name *.tmp from src:local() lookups on Windows. r=jwatt, a=dsmith\n\nThis is a sad hack, but aims to work around the issue that some\nPDF-related software (Acrobat is suspected but not currently confirmed)\nis potentially polluting the global font collection with re-encoded\nsubsets of standard fonts like Arial, but does not munge the psname;\nthese can then be returned by src:local(...) lookups, which results in\ngarbled or missing text.\n\nIn principle, if such fonts are \"installed\", Firefox is not wrong to use\nthem; it's just a badly-configured system. But given that it seems to be\ncaused by some PDF-handling software, without the user's knowledge, it\nseems worth trying to avoid the problem. Simply skipping the psname of\nany font with family-name *.tmp is highly unlikely to adversely affect\nany real-world content.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D191639", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxDWriteFontList.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "57290f3cf2e79f083a35dc5a1e474628475d82a2", "parents": ["c7af063f1aeae8d646aa65389042d18fb037505f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698782052, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "151": {"changesets": [{"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1779578 part 1: When serializing a11y subtrees, include parent id and index in parent for each Accessible. (ESR)  a=RyanVM\n\nWhen we serialize a subtree, we put it into a flat list.\nPreviously, we included the child count for each Accessible so that we knew how many Accessibels to consume as children when de-serializing.\nWe also de-serialized recursively.\nThis made it very difficult to split serialization across IPDL calls, since we would always end up splitting in the middle of some Accessible's children.\nInstead, we now no longer include the child count, but we do include the parent id and the index of the child in that parent.\nThis means that each Accessible can be de-serialized independently and iteratively, making it possible to split wherever we need to.\nRemoteAccessible creation has also been separated from attachment of the child to its parent, since we will need this when splitting.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D184366\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192439", "files": ["accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp", "accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleChildBase.cpp", "accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleChildBase.h", "accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleParent.cpp", "accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleParent.h", "accessible/ipc/RemoteAccessibleBase.h", "accessible/ipc/other/PDocAccessible.ipdl", "accessible/ipc/other/RemoteAccessible.h", "accessible/ipc/win/PDocAccessible.ipdl", "accessible/ipc/win/RemoteAccessible.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "96f7ba066d9a22e6752442ea7f5459cd01189bb6", "parents": ["57290f3cf2e79f083a35dc5a1e474628475d82a2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1779578 part 2: Split serialization of a11y subtrees across multiple IPDL calls if we are likely to exceed the IPDL maximum message size. (ESR)  a=RyanVM\n\nIn the content process, we simply split into multiple calls when the number of Accessibles exceeds our maximum.\nThe maximum is calculated to allow for every Accessible to consume 2 KB in the IPDL message.\nCurrently, this means we split every 131072 Accessibles.\nOf course, we could still exceed this IPDL message size if one or more  Accessibles consumed a lot more than this; e.g. many labels longer than 2 KB.\nHowever, this seems unlikely in the real world.\nIf this turns out to be a problem, we'll need to count the actual size of the serialized data for each Accessible.\nFor example, we could use AccAttributes::SizeOfExcludingThis, though that isn't exactly the serialized size.\nI worry though that such data structure traversal could get expensive at scale.\n\nIn the parent process, we defer attaching the root of the new subtree to its parent until the final call.\nThis is achieved by saving the root during the first call and using that to attach and fire events in the final call.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D184367\n\nDepends on D192439\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192440", "files": ["accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleChildBase.cpp", "accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleParent.cpp", "accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleParent.h", "accessible/ipc/other/PDocAccessible.ipdl", "accessible/ipc/win/PDocAccessible.ipdl", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser.ini", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser_caching_large_update.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2b5c24b04de1086ab70d4088f0953c24b0a72c90", "parents": ["96f7ba066d9a22e6752442ea7f5459cd01189bb6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1848991: Attach a RemoteAccessible to its parent before calling ProxyCreated. (ESR)  a=RyanVM\n\nThis is what we did before the fix for bug 1779578.\nFailure to do this meant that RemoteAccessible::IsLink() returned false even for a child of a HyperText Accessible, which meant the ATK object was created without the HyperLink interface.\nThis change requires that we move the handling of pending OOP child docs, since we can't add a child document until ProxyCreated has been called on the OuterDoc.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D186423\n\nDepends on D192440\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192441", "files": ["accessible/atk/AccessibleWrap.cpp", "accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleParent.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3c5f213db2ea1a237ffe4e206382e8e3b4f6d5c8", "parents": ["2b5c24b04de1086ab70d4088f0953c24b0a72c90"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698849496, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "152": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr115 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings - a=repo-update, r=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192556", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/devtools-compatibility-browsers.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/search-telemetry-v2.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "344e0a63ed3149a2debc4aed0b0626fac3971426", "parents": ["3c5f213db2ea1a237ffe4e206382e8e3b4f6d5c8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1698932136, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "153": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr115 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings tld-suffixes - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D192824", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c75154a3e23068acbe7258deddbe326d6d0b268c", "parents": ["344e0a63ed3149a2debc4aed0b0626fac3971426"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1644612 - Add a height and cleanup languages listbox styling. a=RyanVM\n\nThe \"righter\" way to do this is adding a bunch of min-height: 0 to the\ngrid, the dialog, the content box, etc. But this is more similar to what\nother dialogs do.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D180890", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/dialogs/browserLanguages.xhtml", "browser/components/preferences/dialogs/languages.xhtml", "browser/themes/shared/preferences/preferences.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d87c7891b0c78373d110f17cfe8346d626ef8f24", "parents": ["c75154a3e23068acbe7258deddbe326d6d0b268c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1858570 - Fix relative URL path starting with multiple slashes r=necko-reviewers,kershaw a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D190784", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ec15c0924e3973d5e1afb6117039964d233ad